WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
On 6 August 1945, a nuclear
weapon was used on Hiroshima.

2
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.410
On 9 August, on Nagasaki.

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.370
They remain the only nuclear
weapons ever used in war.

4
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.440
Yet some states still
keep them, ready to use,

5
00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.170
so that no enemy dares attack.

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.280
So if a weapon keeps the peace
only because it is never used,

7
00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.860
is owning it right or wrong?

8
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:29.930
In this mission, you'll see how a utilitarian
might weigh decades of peace against

9
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.050
a small chance of catastrophic suffering.

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.230
Then you'll build an
argument map on one question:

11
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.220
can nuclear deterrence be justified?

12
00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.200
Your mission: weigh up whether owning a
weapon that must never be used is right

13
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.010
or wrong.
